7. VISUALIZING CLUSTERS AND INSIGHTS

WEKA allows users to visualize the clusters using scatter plots. Visualization helps identify similarities, differences, overlaps, and possible patterns among instances.

Procedure

1. Load the dataset in WEKA Explorer.
2. Open the Cluster panel.
3. Select "SimpleKMeans".
4. Set the required number of clusters and run the algorithm.
5. In the result list, right-click the clustering result.
6. Select Visualize cluster assignments.
7. Choose the attributes to display on the X-axis and Y-axis.
8. Observe the scatter plot and the different colors representing the clusters.
9. Repeat the procedure for different values of K.

Interpreting the Scatter Plot

- Different colors: Represent different cluster assignments.
- Separated groups: Indicate that the selected attributes may distinguish the clusters clearly.
- Overlapping points: Indicate that some instances have similar attribute values across clusters.
- Cluster distribution: Shows how instances are spread across the selected attributes.

For the Iris dataset, petal length and petal width can help reveal groupings among the flower instances. Some species may be well separated, while others may overlap.

