9. RESULT

Clustering of datasets was performed successfully using WEKA Explorer. The SimpleKMeans algorithm was executed with different numbers of clusters, and the resulting cluster assignments, centroids, and SSE values were studied. Other clustering techniques, including EM, Hierarchical Clustering, and COBWEB, were also explored. Cluster visualizations were used to understand the distribution, separation, and overlap of data instances.

10. CONCLUSION

Clustering is a useful unsupervised learning technique for discovering hidden patterns and natural groupings in datasets without predefined class labels. WEKA provides a convenient interface for applying clustering algorithms, comparing different cluster configurations, and visualizing the results. Selecting an appropriate algorithm and number of clusters helps produce meaningful and interpretable groups.
